2025-05-05 00:59:41 - Thread-490 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Below is a sequence of illustrative BigQuery SQL statements – from exploratory “look-around” queries to the final one that pin-points the provider who records the single-largest combined average cost for outpatient and inpatient services in 2014.

```sql
-- 1. Quick peek at the data structure and a few rows
SELECT
  npi,
  nppes_provider_last_org_name AS last_name,
  nppes_provider_first_name    AS first_name,
  place_of_service,
  average_medicare_allowed_amt
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. What values actually appear in `place_of_service`?
SELECT DISTINCT place_of_service
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Get a feel for outpatient (“O”) records with their allowed amount
SELECT
  npi,
  last_name,
  first_name,
  average_medicare_allowed_amt
FROM (
  SELECT
    npi,
    nppes_provider_last_org_name AS last_name,
    nppes_provider_first_name    AS first_name,
    average_medicare_allowed_amt
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
  WHERE place_of_service = 'O'
  ORDER BY average_medicare_allowed_amt DESC
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Likewise for inpatient (“I”) records
SELECT
  npi,
  last_name,
  first_name,
  average_medicare_allowed_amt
FROM (
  SELECT
    npi,
    nppes_provider_last_org_name AS last_name,
    nppes_provider_first_name    AS first_name,
    average_medicare_allowed_amt
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
  WHERE place_of_service = 'I'
  ORDER BY average_medicare_allowed_amt DESC
)
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Total OUTPATIENT average-allowed amounts per provider
SELECT
  npi,
  ANY_VALUE(nppes_provider_last_org_name) AS last_name,
  ANY_VALUE(nppes_provider_first_name)    AS first_name,
  SUM(average_medicare_allowed_amt)       AS outpatient_allowed_sum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
WHERE place_of_service = 'O'
GROUP BY npi
ORDER BY outpatient_allowed_sum DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Total INPATIENT average-allowed amounts per provider
SELECT
  npi,
  ANY_VALUE(nppes_provider_last_org_name) AS last_name,
  ANY_VALUE(nppes_provider_first_name)    AS first_name,
  SUM(average_medicare_allowed_amt)       AS inpatient_allowed_sum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
WHERE place_of_service = 'I'
GROUP BY npi
ORDER BY inpatient_allowed_sum DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Combine both settings for every provider
SELECT
  npi,
  ANY_VALUE(nppes_provider_last_org_name) AS last_name,
  ANY_VALUE(nppes_provider_first_name)    AS first_name,
  SUM(CASE WHEN place_of_service = 'O' THEN average_medicare_allowed_amt ELSE 0 END) AS outpatient_allowed_sum,
  SUM(CASE WHEN place_of_service = 'I' THEN average_medicare_allowed_amt ELSE 0 END) AS inpatient_allowed_sum,
  SUM(average_medicare_allowed_amt)                                                   AS combined_allowed_sum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
GROUP BY npi
ORDER BY combined_allowed_sum DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Final: the single provider with the highest combined outpatient + inpatient AVERAGE Medicare allowed amount
SELECT
  npi,
  nppes_provider_last_org_name AS last_name,
  nppes_provider_first_name    AS first_name,
  SUM(CASE WHEN place_of_service = 'O' THEN average_medicare_allowed_amt ELSE 0 END) AS outpatient_allowed_sum,
  SUM(CASE WHEN place_of_service = 'I' THEN average_medicare_allowed_amt ELSE 0 END) AS inpatient_allowed_sum,
  SUM(average_medicare_allowed_amt)                                                   AS combined_allowed_sum
FROM `bigquery-public-data.cms_medicare.physicians_and_other_supplier_2014`
GROUP BY npi, last_name, first_name
ORDER BY combined_allowed_sum DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

Running the last query will return the NPI and name of the healthcare provider whose total of average Medicare-allowed amounts across both outpatient and inpatient settings is the highest for calendar year 2014.
